  <!-- 1.16.0 -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="v1.16.0">
    <h2>v1.16.0</h2>
    <p><strong>Theme Switcher, AA Colours, Section, Footer, Links & Scroll Reveal, Framework-Ready JS</strong></p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>New Components:
  - Theme Toggle — data-sui-theme-toggle on any button toggles dark mode;
    ="light" / "dark" / "system" set a value; &lt;html data-sui-theme-auto&gt;
    follows the OS with no button. Saves the choice, follows the OS until
    the user picks, syncs across tabs. SoftUI.theme.get/set/toggle/clear/
    system and a sui-theme-change event ({theme, source}). New
    sui-theme-toggle sun/moon button (-sm, -lg)
  - Scroll Reveal — sui-reveal with -start, -end, -down, -fade, -scale,
    -zoom-out, -blur; speeds sui-reveal-fast / -slow; --sui-reveal-blur;
    data-reveal-stagger, data-reveal-repeat, --sui-delay,
    --sui-reveal-distance, --sui-reveal-duration and SoftUI.reveal().
    Content stays visible without JS, under reduced motion and in print
  - Section — sui-section / sui-section-sm page spacing, sui-section-header
    with sui-section-title, sui-section-subtitle, sui-section-action, and
    sui-heading-accent. Sizes sui-section-sm / -lg; surfaces
    sui-section-raised, -inset, -alt, -bordered; sui-section-header-center
    and -bordered; heading accent colours (-success, -danger, -warning,
    -info), -lg and -bottom
  - Footer — centred, split (sui-footer-split) and multi-column
    (sui-footer-columns), bordered / raised / inset / tinted, compact
    (sui-footer-sm), raised links and social icons (sui-footer-social)
  - Links — sui-link (underlined prose link), sui-link-subtle,
    sui-link-muted, sui-link-arrow (RTL-aware), sui-link-external,
    sui-link-raised, sui-link-underline-hover, colours (-success, -danger,
    -warning, -info) and sizes (-sm, -lg)
  - Status Dot — sui-status-dot with colours, -sm / -lg, -pulse, and a
    sui-status label wrapper

New:
  - Hero: sui-hero-start (start-aligned) and sui-hero-split (text + media
    side by side from 992px: sui-hero-content, sui-hero-media,
    sui-hero-media-start)
  - Display headings: sui-display-1, -2, -3 (fluid)
  - Stat card footer: sui-stat-footer pill with a --sui-fill bar and
    -primary / -success / -danger / -warning / -info tints
  - Avatars: sui-avatar-2xl (120px) and sui-avatar-3xl (160px)
  - sui-flat-all — on a container, turns every neumorphic shadow inside
    (including toggle knobs and range thumbs) into a hairline outline
  - Spacing scale 0-7 (0/4/8/16/24/48/64/96px) backed by --sui-space-0..7.
    New sui-px/py/pt/pb/ps/pe-*, sui-mx/my/ms/me-*, sui-my-auto,
    sui-gap-6 and sui-gap-7. Start/end classes flip in RTL; sui-ml-* and
    sui-mr-* stay as aliases of ms/me
  - Font utilities: sui-font-sans, sui-font-mono, sui-tabular-nums,
    sui-proportional-nums
  - Images: sui-img-fluid, sui-img-frame. Aspect ratio: sui-aspect-4-5
  - Sidebar: off-canvas drawer below 900px (data-sidebar-open,
    data-sidebar-close, overlay, Esc), sui-sidebar-static,
    sui-sidebar-drawer, sui-sidebar-trigger-mobile, and
    SoftUI.sidebar().open() / close() / isOpen()
  - Tokens: --sui-{primary,success,danger,warning,info}-text and -text-hover
    (AA text shades), --sui-warning-contrast, --sui-font-mono,
    --sui-space-0..7, --sui-section-space / -sm / -lg / -xs,
    --sui-section-header-gap. Optional: --sui-focus-ring,
    --sui-focus-ring-color, --sui-link, --sui-link-hover,
    --sui-link-underline, --sui-heading-accent
  - Embed build: dist/softui-embed.css and softui-embed.min.css. Same
    components and tokens, without the global reset, body styles, element
    typography, scrollbar, reduced-motion and print rules outside SoftUI
    elements
  - window.SoftUI is a real global and the package's CommonJS / ES default
    export (import SoftUI from 'softui-css'). Importing on the server (SSR)
    is a no-op; loading the script twice reuses the first copy
  - SoftUI.init(root) sets up markup added after load (element, selector or
    nothing; safe to repeat). SoftUI.version
  - A component that fails to initialise logs "[SoftUI] &lt;name&gt; failed"
    and no longer stops the others
  - SoftUI.modal(), SoftUI.sheet() and SoftUI.carousel() accept an element
  - Typewriter and Text Rotate: data-reserve (fixed width), data-sr-text
  - New events: sui-copy, sui-copy-error, sui-tree-toggle, sui-diff-change

Changes (check these when upgrading):
  - Coloured text uses the new -text shades: links, outline and ghost
    buttons, outline badges and chips, alerts, sui-text-*, steppers, toasts
    and active nav. Darker in light mode (warning text is now brown),
    lighter in dark mode (link hover gets lighter, not darker). If you
    rebrand --sui-primary, also set --sui-primary-text and -text-hover in
    each theme
  - Success and info fills are slightly darker so white text passes AA:
    --sui-success #1FA96E → #198758 (hover #178A59 → #126D47),
    --sui-info #1A82D4 → #187AC8 (hover #146BAE → #1364A3)
  - --sui-text-light: #6A7D94 → #526072 (light), #8A94A6 → #939CAD (dark)
  - --sui-text-muted (light): #5A6A7E → #4D5A6D, so muted text also passes
    AA on --sui-bg-dark
  - Dark-mode warning fills (buttons, badges, chips, filled alerts) use dark
    text (#2D3748) instead of white
  - Tints, glows and focus rings use color-mix() and follow your colour
    tokens at any scope. Old-palette tints now match the current palette
    (slightly deeper); the info chart colour is now --sui-info.
    Browser baseline for these effects: Chrome/Edge 111, Safari 16.2,
    Firefox 113. Older browsers lose tints and rings; layout is unaffected
  - Spacing (sui-p-*, sui-m-*, ...), text colour and alignment (sui-text-*),
    radius (sui-rounded-*) and aspect-ratio (sui-aspect-*) utilities now use
    !important, like display, flex and gap. They now override component
    defaults (e.g. sui-modal-body sui-p-0) and inline margin/padding on the
    same element. Custom CSS that overrode them at equal specificity now
    needs !important
  - Gutter classes sui-g-*, sui-gx-* and sui-gy-* now apply (a default rule
    used to force a 24px horizontal, 0 vertical gutter). sui-g-0 is now
    flush, g-1/2/3 are narrower, g-5 is wider, and g/gy rows get vertical
    gaps between wrapped lines
  - All component events now bubble. New sui-* aliases: sui-editable-save,
    sui-editable-cancel, sui-countdown-end (editable:save, editable:cancel
    and countdown:end still fire)
  - Toast title/message and tour title/description are inserted as plain
    text (XSS fix). Pass html: true for trusted HTML. File upload names are
    always text
  - Escape closes only the topmost modal or sheet; static modals, alert
    dialogs and static sheets shake instead of closing. An open dropdown,
    popover, menu, combobox, styled select, speed dial or lightbox inside
    it is closed first, on its own Escape
  - sui-mx-auto and sui-my-auto moved into the spacing utilities, before the
    single-side classes, so sui-mx-auto sui-ms-3 now gives a 16px start
    margin (sui-ms-auto / sui-me-auto still win over sui-ms-* / sui-me-*)
  - Sidebars become an off-canvas drawer below 900px; add
    sui-sidebar-static to keep one inline
  - Navigation menu: clicking a sub-menu parent opens/closes its sub-menu
    instead of following its link
  - Scripted motion respects prefers-reduced-motion: carousel autoplay,
    text rotate, typewriter, radial count-up, scroll reveal, and
    scrollspy/tour smooth scrolling
  - data-theme sets color-scheme, so native scrollbars and form controls
    match the theme
  - Scoped themes fully reset component tints, the select arrow, borders,
    scrollbars, warning text and the loading overlay; the overlay follows
    the theme background
  - code, kbd, OTP slots, colour picker, copy input and calendar time use
    --sui-font-mono. --sui-font also lists 'Plus Jakarta Sans Variable'
  - The hero title scales smoothly (clamp) instead of jumping at 600px
  - Typewriter block and underscore cursors blink; text already in the
    element is kept and typed over
  - Playground preview iframe no longer has allow-same-origin, so shared
    #code= links cannot run script against the docs site

Fixes:
  - Badge dot inside sui-badge-positioned is a 10px dot (was an 18px pill);
    added the info dot colour
  - Cards: images keep their aspect ratio and match the card radius;
    overlay cards are positioned and clipped automatically; cards drop
    their padding for direct images; sui-card-horizontal is a real row
  - Outline toggle group border and default sidebar shadow restored
  - Printing a dark page (or a scoped dark section) uses the light palette
  - Focus returns to the opener on every modal/sheet close; body scroll
    unlocks only when no overlay is open
  - Opening a modal or sheet moves focus into it (it stayed on the opener),
    and Tab pulls focus back inside if it has escaped
  - SoftUI.carousel(el) returns the existing instance instead of building a
    second one with its own position, listeners and autoplay timer
  - Command dialog open buttons added after load work
  - Inset sidebars get a solid background when shown as a drawer
  - Drawer drag-to-dismiss threw an error and left the drawer open
  - Carousel: autoplay intervals no longer stack; rewind-mode dots and
    goTo() stop at the last full page
  - Datepicker in 24-hour mode no longer adds "AM"
  - Copy button: falls back to execCommand (works over http), restores its
    own icon or label, survives double-clicks, .copy-failed state
  - Password toggle no longer swallows click events
  - Countdown: an invalid data-date shows "--"; a past date no longer
    throws; relative dates may contain spaces ("+2y 5d")
  - Timeline compact + right / alternate margins
  - Stack back cards show inside surfaces and cards (isolation)
  - Tour no longer dims the highlighted target
  - Bottom-centre toasts slide up from the bottom edge
  - Text rotate exit animation in RTL
  - RTL via logical properties: navbar brand, timeline, alerts, filled
    alerts, blockquotes, table headers and corners, sortable data table
    headers, lists, bordered stats, positioned badges, avatar status dots,
    navigation menu

Accessibility:
  - Contrast: coloured text (-text tokens) meets WCAG AA 4.5:1 on every
    --sui-bg* surface in light and dark; text on filled buttons, badges and
    chips meets 4.5:1 (white, or #2D3748 on warning)
  - Keyboard support and roles: rating (slider), colour swatches (radio
    group), tree view (ARIA tree), editable text (button), lightbox (dialog
    with focus trap), diff (slider), navigation menu (arrows, Esc,
    aria-expanded), sidebar drawer (focus trap, Esc)
  - Focus-visible rings: dock, swap, speed dial, data table selects,
    calendar AM/PM, copy buttons, colour swatches, navigation menu;
    context-menu items reached by keyboard get the hover highlight
  - Speed dial: aria-expanded, Escape closes it, closed actions leave the
    tab order; dock and speed-dial labels show on focus
  - Typewriter and text rotate: screen readers hear the full text once,
    without the cursor glyph
  - Scroll reveal: hidden content appears when it receives focus, and short
    elements at the very end of the page are revealed
  - Vertical diff slider: PageUp/PageDown move the handle the same way as
    the Up/Down arrows
  - Playground editor is no longer a keyboard trap (Esc then Tab leaves)

Docs:
  - New pages: Section, Links, Footer, Scroll Reveal
  - Pages changed in this release keep demos uncluttered: short captions,
    with keys, attributes, events and tokens in a Reference table
  - New sections: Hero (Start Aligned, Split), Typography (Display), Stat
    Card (With Footer), Badges (Status Dot), Shadows (Flat Scope), Avatars
    (2XL/3XL), Sidebar (Mobile Drawer), Timeline (RTL), Spacing, Text,
    Sizing (Images), Aspect Ratio (4:5), Typewriter / Text Rotate (Reserve
    Space)
  - Theming: theme switcher, text shades, tints and focus rings, link and
    section tokens, dark-theme halo note, loading the fonts
  - Getting Started: JS API, frameworks with SoftUI.init, events, embed
    build; the JS size is measured at build time
  - The no-flash snippet no longer hides the body with opacity:0, so it
    also works with the embed build
  - Fixed "On This Page" links on Alerts, Badges, Buttons, Cards, Progress
    and Toggles; fixed Playground snippets with non-existent classes
  - 118 playground snippets (new: Theme Toggle, Hero Split, Section &amp;
    Header, Stat Card Footer, Status Dot, Footer, Scroll Reveal, Links)
  - The docs footer uses sui-footer

Tooling:
  - npm run build:embed; build:min also builds the embed files and syncs
    the "/*! SoftUI vX.Y.Z" banners and SoftUI.version from package.json
  - Publish workflow checks the npm registry, installs with
    bun --frozen-lockfile and can be run manually; npm run dev works on
    Windows cmd.exe</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 1.15.0 -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="v1.15.0">
    <h2>v1.15.0</h2>
